Summary: [8/9 Regression] too few arguments to function when sfinae on calling pointer to member function
Status: RESOLVED
Severity: normal
Reporter: gufideg@gmail.com
Created: 2018-05-22T03:44:56Z

Description:
This code fails under GCC 8:

    #include <utility>

    template<typename...>
    using void_t = void;

    template<typename U, typename V,
    void_t<decltype(
        (std::declval<U>().*std::declval<V>())()
    )>* = nullptr>
    void boom(){}

    struct Foo {
        void bar(){}
    };

    int main() {
        boom<Foo, decltype(&Foo::bar)>();
    }

This particular code compiles on all other GCC versions since 4.7
It also compiles on all versions of clang since version 3.4

Live example: https://godbolt.org/g/viHnMn

