bug_content:
Title: clang-format option for ignoring first column comments
State: open
Labels: clang-format, bugzilla
Reporter: llvmbot
Created: 2016-03-01T08:53:25Z

Description:
|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| Bugzilla Link | [26781](https://llvm.org/bz26781) |
| Version | unspecified |
| OS | Linux |
| Reporter | LLVM Bugzilla Contributor |

## Extended Description 
Description of the problem
Sometimes first column ASCII art comments or code disabled by comment shouldn't be re-indented but currently there's no method to have clang-format leave them alone.

Steps to reproduce:
1. Create cf.c:
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stdint.h>

typedef bool boolean_t;

int main()
{
/*======================================================================
 * Function: Main
 *======================================================================*/

    uint64_t u = 1;
    int *i;
//  int j;
    boolean_t b = 0;

    return 0;
}
2. Read http://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormatStyleOptions.html for options.
2. Run
clang-format -style='{BasedOnStyle: WebKit, AlignConsecutiveAssignments: true, AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: true, PointerAlignment: Right}' cf.c

Desired result:
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stdint.h>

typedef bool boolean_t;

int main()
{
/*======================================================================
 * Function: Main
 *======================================================================*/

    uint64_t  u = 1;
    int       *i;
//  int j;
    boolean_t  b = 0;

    return 0;
}

Actual result:
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stdint.h>

typedef bool boolean_t;

int main()
{
    /*======================================================================
 * Function: Main
 *======================================================================*/

    uint64_t u = 1;
    int *    i;
    //  int j;
    boolean_t b = 0;

    return 0;
}

The first line of the block comment has been re-indented, the commented out initialisation was re-indented and the commented out code wasn't skipped when aligning following code.

I guess there's an argument that says if you leave the following lines of a block comment alone you should leave the first line alone too but it seems easier to add the option to not re-indent first column comments and to pretend they aren't there for alignment purposes.

--- Comment #1 by llvmbot at 2016-11-28T08:20:56Z ---
Still here in
clang version 3.9.0 (branches/release_39 280336)

