Title: aarch64 inline asm: miscompilation depending on function parameters order
State: closed
Labels: invalid, clang, bugzilla
Reporter: llvmbot
Created: 2021-02-24T19:58:19Z

Description:
|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| Bugzilla Link | [49343](https://llvm.org/bz49343) |
| Resolution | INVALID |
| Resolved on | Feb 24, 2021 12:05 |
| Version | trunk |
| OS | All |
| Reporter | LLVM Bugzilla Contributor |
| CC | @topperc,@zygoloid |

## Extended Description 
compiler explorer link: https://godbolt.org/z/e9n49n

code:

#include <arm_neon.h>

// output:
//         smlal   v0.4s, v1.4h, v2.4h  
int32x4_t good(int32x4_t acc, int16x4_t x, int16x4_t y) {
    asm("smlal %[acc].4s, %[x].4h, %[y].4h"
        : [acc]"=w"(acc)
        : [x]"w"(x),
          [y]"w"(y)
        :);
    return acc;
}

// output:
//         smlal   v0.4s, v0.4h, v1.4h
// bug: v0 is used for both x and y arguments!
int32x4_t bad(int16x4_t x, int16x4_t y, int32x4_t acc) {
    asm("smlal %[acc].4s, %[x].4h, %[y].4h"
        : [acc]"=w"(acc)
        : [x]"w"(x),
          [y]"w"(y)
        :);
    return acc;
}

--- Comment #1 by llvmbot at 2021-02-24T20:05:15Z ---
Oops! Thanks so much, that's true :-) sorry, closing.

--- Comment #2 by topperc at 2021-02-24T20:03:35Z ---
I think you want to use "+w" rather than "=w" for acc. That tells the compiler that acc is an input and an output. "=w" just says its an output.

