Summary: Can't define member function out of line with non-type template parameter
Status: RESOLVED
Severity: normal
Reporter: barry.revzin@gmail.com
Created: 2019-12-03T19:04:25Z

Description:
From StackOverflow (https://stackoverflow.com/q/59163716/2069064):

struct A {};

template <A a>
struct B {
    void f();
};

template <A a>
void B<a>::f() { }

On the gcc trunk on godbolt, this fails with:

<source>:9:14: error: invalid use of incomplete type 'struct B<((const A)a)>'
    9 | void B<a>::f() { }
      |              ^
<source>:4:8: note: declaration of 'struct B<((const A)a)>'
    4 | struct B {
      |        ^

But compiles fine if you replace the declaration of A with something like "using A = int;"

