Created attachment 45814
gcc9-pr89481.patch

Untested fix for -std=c++2a compilation.

--- Comment #3 by mickey.veksler@gmail.com at 2019-02-25T15:13:06Z ---
Thanks for looking into it.

With the fix, does it behave the same way for:
 - runtime evaluation of all_zeros()
 - compile time evaluation such as std::integral_constant<bool, all_zeros()>::value;

Currently (trunk 20190223 (experimental) with -std=c++2a), it returns different results for both cases, which does not feel right.

