Summary: [5/6 Regression] Wrong code with pointer-to-member
Status: RESOLVED
Severity: normal
Reporter: reichelt@gcc.gnu.org
Created: 2017-02-23T10:14:43Z

Description:
The following code snippet is miscompiled since GCC 6:

======================================
struct A
{
  char c;
};

int main()
{
  char A::* p = &A::c;
  static char A::* const q = p;

  A a;
  return &(a.*q) - &a.c;
}
======================================

The program should return 0, but doesn't.

--- Comment #1 by trippels@gcc.gnu.org at 2017-02-23T10:25:51Z ---
Started with gcc-5 for me.

--- Comment #2 by mpolacek@gcc.gnu.org at 2017-02-23T10:27:47Z ---
