bug_content:
Title: BreakBeforeBraces affects class but not struct
State: closed
Labels: clang-format, bugzilla
Reporter: steveire
Created: 2014-11-18T18:51:05Z

Description:
|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| Bugzilla Link | [21595](https://llvm.org/bz21595) |
| Resolution | FIXED |
| Resolved on | Aug 01, 2018 03:52 |
| Version | trunk |
| OS | All |

## Extended Description 
Clang format formats structs and classes differently:

$ cat style.cpp 

class AAA {

};

struct BBB {

};

void someFun() {
	if (true)
	 {
		return;
	}
	 else
	 {
	  return;
	}
}
$ clang-format -style="{BreakBeforeBraces: Linux}" style.cpp 

class AAA
{
};

struct BBB {
};

void someFun()
{
  if (true) {
    return;
  } else {
    return;
  }
}


This is weird and undesirable. Please extend clang-format with an option to allow putting the brace on the following line for structs. It doesn't matter what it is called, and I have seen http://llvm.org/bugs/show_bug.cgi?id=20587 .

Thanks!

--- Comment #1 by steveire at 2018-08-01T10:52:12Z ---
This was apparently implemented at some point. The following style breaks after both classes and structs:

-style="{BreakBeforeBraces: Custom, BraceWrapping: {AfterStruct : true, AfterClass: true} }"

--- Comment #2 by llvmbot at 2016-06-24T14:20:11Z ---
The same goes for unions when BreakBeforeBraces: Allman. ex.

typedef union {
    struct
    {
        uint32_t put : 1;
        uint32_t get : 1;
    };
    uint8_t byte;
} cAccessList_blockIdAccess_t;

should have been

typedef union 
{
    struct
    {
        uint32_t put : 1;
        uint32_t get : 1;
    };
    uint8_t byte;
} cAccessList_blockIdAccess_t;

--- Comment #3 by llvmbot at 2016-06-24T10:34:17Z ---
The same formatting "error" happens in BreakBeforeBraces: Allman. Which I expect all '{' to be on new line as example

structType_t structName = 
{
    .memberOne = 1,
    .memberTwo = 1)
};

but clang moves the '{' up.

structType_t structName = {
    .memberOne = 1,
    .memberTwo = 1)
};

--- Comment #4 by llvmbot at 2014-12-09T10:10:15Z ---
Yes, as mentioned before, this was intentionally changed after llvm/llvm-project#20961 . Sorry for the inconvenience. There is also no easy way for us to undo that.

--- Comment #5 by llvmbot at 2014-12-09T10:08:25Z ---
In clang-format 3.5 and earlier versions this worked as expected, ie formatting structs and classes in the same way. Are there any kind of work around? We currently have a couple of Windows developers running 3.6 and some Linux developers running 3.5.

Thanks!

--- Comment #6 by llvmbot at 2014-11-19T14:09:02Z ---
There has been the idea to provide flags for each single brace decision and have the current options just as "presets". I don't think anyone is actively working on it, though.

