Summary: [12/13 regression][rejects valid] invalid use of auto when deducing return type of base class template
Status: RESOLVED
Severity: normal
Reporter: joeloser@fastmail.com
Created: 2022-05-16T21:35:50Z

Description:
The following code used to work in GCC 11.3.0, but fails on GCC 12.1.0 and trunk.

```
#include <string_view>

constexpr auto g(auto name_fn)  {
    return name_fn();
}

template <char... Cs> struct ct_string {
    static constexpr char str[] = {Cs..., 0};
    static constexpr auto name() { return std::string_view{str, sizeof...(Cs)}; }
};

struct S : ct_string<'f', 'o', 'o'> {
    constexpr auto f() {
        return g(name);
    }
};

int main() {
    {
        S s;
        [[maybe_unused]] constexpr auto name = s.f();
    }

    return 0;
}
```


This code works on GCC 11.3.0 but fails on GCC 12.1.0 onward, including trunk. See it live at https://godbolt.org/z/9c8vb1eP5

One workaround is to explicitly provide the return type for `ct_string::foo` static function such as at https://godbolt.org/z/ccqPxoM5P which works on GCC 11.3.0, 12.1.0, and trunk.

