Commit Message:
c++: extend -Wself-move for mem-init-list [PR109396]

We already warn for:

  x = std::move (x);

which triggers:

  warning: moving 'x' of type 'int' to itself [-Wself-move]

but bug 109396 reports that this doesn't work for a member-initializer-list:

  X() : x(std::move (x))

so this patch amends that.

	PR c++/109396

