| OS | Linux |
| Reporter | LLVM Bugzilla Contributor |

## Extended Description 
Thanks for a great compiler that is steadily improving!

Inline assembly with MMX registers is fragile. It's unusual to use MMX registers so I'm likely exercising previously untested code paths.

Here are a couple of examples that fail:

```
//Example 1
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdio.h>

typedef uint8_t mmx_t __attribute__ ((vector_size (8)));

int main(void) {
  register mmx_t mmx asm ("mm0");
  asm volatile ("" : "+y" (mmx));
  printf("%d\n", mmx[0]);
  return 0;
}
```

